.TH KLVTOOL-EXTRACT 1 "1970-01-01" "klvtool dev" "User Commands"
.SH "NAME"
klvtool\-extract \- Extract raw KLV/data payloads from an MPEG\-TS file and write a manifest.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
klvtool extract \-\-input <file.ts> \-\-out <dir> [\-\-view auto|pretty|raw]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Validate backend availability and extract raw KLV/data PES payloads from an MPEG\-TS file. Each payload is written as a separate file under <out>, with one NDJSON line per record appended to <out>/manifest.ndjson capturing transport metadata (PID, packet offset, PTS/DTS), payload location, and a SHA\-256 hash for chain\-of\-custody. Use this when you need preserved raw artifacts for `klvtool packetize`, downstream forensics, or bug reports.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR
MPEG\-TS input path
.TP
\fB\-\-out\fR
output directory for extracted payloads and manifest.ndjson
.TP
\fB\-\-view\fR \fI(default auto)\fR
presentation mode: auto, pretty, or raw
.SH "OUTPUT FORMAT"
Each invocation writes payload files under <out>/ plus a manifest.ndjson file with one Record per line.
.SS Fields
.TP
\fBschemaVersion\fR (string)
manifest envelope version
.TP
\fBsourceInputPath\fR (string)
the \-\-input path as provided, captured for chain of custody
.TP
\fBbackendName\fR (string)
extraction backend name (e.g. "ffmpeg")
.TP
\fBbackendVersion\fR (string)
detected backend version
.TP
\fBrecords[].recordId\fR (string)
stable identifier; matches the payload filename stem
.TP
\fBrecords[].pid\fR (integer)
MPEG\-TS PID this payload came from
.TP
\fBrecords[].transportStreamId\fR (integer)
TS ID if the program map carried one
.TP
\fBrecords[].packetOffset\fR (integer; bytes)
byte offset of the originating TS packet
.TP
\fBrecords[].packetIndex\fR (integer)
0\-based index of the originating TS packet
.TP
\fBrecords[].continuityCounter\fR (integer)
TS continuity counter value at extraction
.TP
\fBrecords[].pts\fR (integer; 90 kHz ticks)
PES PTS if present (transport\-relative; not wall\-clock)
.TP
\fBrecords[].dts\fR (integer; 90 kHz ticks)
PES DTS if present
.TP
\fBrecords[].payloadPath\fR (string)
relative path to the extracted payload file under <out>
.TP
\fBrecords[].payloadSize\fR (integer; bytes)
.TP
\fBrecords[].payloadHash\fR (string)
SHA\-256 hex digest of the payload bytes
.TP
\fBrecords[].warnings\fR (array)
extraction\-time warnings (empty array if clean)
.SS Time semantics
PTS/DTS are MPEG\-TS transport timestamps in 90 kHz ticks, relative to an unspecified clock origin. They are not wall\-clock; use them to order payloads, not to correlate against a real\-world event. For wall\-clock, decode the metadata stream and read MISB ST 0601 tag 2.
.SS Schema stability
Manifest schema is stable within klvtool 1.x: new fields are additive.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
Extract all data\-stream payloads to a directory
.RS 4
.nf
$ klvtool extract --input mission.ts --out ./mission-extract
.fi
.RE
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
success
.TP
\fB1\fR
transport read failure, output write failure, or backend unavailable
.TP
\fB2\fR
invalid usage
.SH "ENVIRONMENT"
.TP
\fBNO_COLOR\fR
disable ANSI color in pretty output
.SH "FILES"
.TP
\fB<out>/manifest.ndjson\fR
extraction manifest (one Record per line)
.TP
\fB<out>/<recordId>.bin\fR
raw payload files, one per extracted PES unit
.SH "REQUIRED TOOLS"
ffmpeg, ffprobe
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBklvtool\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-packetize\fR(1),
\fBklvtool\-decode\fR(1)
